  <h2>What VP Infra does differently in residential real estate construction</h2>

  <p>VP Infra starts every residential project with a soil investigation report. Most smaller builders skip this entirely. Soil bearing capacity data directly informs the foundation design, and getting it wrong can cause settlement cracks within three to five years of construction. Not a pleasant conversation to have with your family after spending ₹50 lakh on a house.</p>

  <p>VP Infra uses AAC blocks for all masonry, not conventional red clay bricks. AAC blocks are lighter, more thermally efficient, and better at sound insulation. For a home in Lucknow, where summer temperatures regularly cross 42 degrees Celsius, better thermal insulation directly reduces your air conditioning cost every month.</p>

  <p>All structural concrete is M20 minimum for slabs, M25 for columns and beams, with cube compression test records maintained for every pour. The company also integrates solar-ready infrastructure into new builds at the design stage. Pre-laid conduits, load-bearing parapet planning, and roof orientation are handled before construction begins, so adding <a href="/services/solar-installation/">solar panels</a> later is a simple plug-in rather than a messy retrofit.</p>

