  <h2>Frequently asked questions about real estate builders in Lucknow</h2>

  <h3>What is the RERA registration requirement for builders in Lucknow?</h3>

  <p>Under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act 2016, developers selling units in a project exceeding 500 sq mt or 8 units must register with UP RERA. This applies to developers selling units in a planned project, not to builders constructing on a client's own plot under a private construction contract. If you're buying into a society or apartment block, always verify UP RERA registration at rera.up.gov.in before payment.</p>

  <h3>How do real estate builders in Lucknow typically price their services?</h3>

  <p>Most builders price residential construction on a per-square-foot basis for the built-up area, with a separate line for premium items like modular kitchens, elevators, and high-end fixtures. A transparent builder provides a detailed Bill of Quantities (BOQ) listing every material by grade, brand, and quantity before you sign. If a builder gives you only a lump sum without a BOQ, that's a negotiating tactic that almost never works in your favour.</p>

  <h3>Can VP Infra handle projects outside Lucknow city limits?</h3>

  <p>VP Infra Properties takes projects across Uttar Pradesh, with Lucknow as the primary base. Locations within reasonable distance of Lucknow including Unnao, Barabanki, Raebareli, and Sitapur have been served. <a href="/contact-us/">Reach out</a> with your specific location for confirmation.</p>

  <h3>What warranty does VP Infra offer on completed construction?</h3>

  <p>VP Infra provides a written structural warranty of 10 years on the RCC framework. Waterproofing carries a 3-year warranty. Plumbing and electrical work is covered for 1 year. All warranty terms are documented in the construction agreement before work begins, not mentioned verbally after handover.</p>

